1
00:00:23,589 --> 00:00:27,427
My heart feels like it's about to burn

2
00:00:27,427 --> 00:00:30,396
But I'm going to forget about that now

3
00:00:30,396 --> 00:00:36,936
I don't need some sort of mundane love

4
00:00:36,936 --> 00:00:42,533
My lips will dry, but I'm going to give up on you

5
00:00:43,042 --> 00:00:46,713
Cooling my passion

6
00:00:46,713 --> 00:00:49,048
I'm waiting for the night to come

7
00:00:49,048 --> 00:00:52,251
I'm going to lure you into a tantalizing trap

8
00:00:52,251 --> 00:00:55,049
Mysterious purple rose

9
00:00:55,288 --> 00:00:58,558
Making the flower petals sway

10
00:00:58,558 --> 00:01:02,119
I will change tomorrow

11
00:01:02,462 --> 00:01:05,556
009-1

12
00:01:08,801 --> 00:01:12,760
Destiny girl forever

13
00:01:15,008 --> 00:01:18,136
009-1

14
00:01:21,347 --> 00:01:25,283
Destiny girl forever

15
00:01:27,653 --> 00:01:30,315
009-1

16
00:02:24,610 --> 00:02:26,512
They say that if you toss a coin
over your shoulder,

17
00:02:26,512 --> 00:02:28,844
you will be able to visit Rome again.

18
00:02:29,682 --> 00:02:32,919
Going along with a mundane tradition
like that isn't all that bad.

19
00:02:32,919 --> 00:02:35,012
It's not too often I get to go on vacation after all.

20
00:02:37,690 --> 00:02:41,091
If you toss two coins over your shoulder,
you'll be united with the one you love.

21
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:44,659
If you toss three, you can dump your partner.

22
00:02:50,203 --> 00:02:53,473
Either way, it doesn't have
anything to do with me.

23
00:02:53,473 --> 00:02:54,872
Thief!

24
00:02:58,478 --> 00:03:00,105
Catch him!

25
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:11,412
I really don't seem to be made
for peace and quiet.

26
00:03:12,758 --> 00:03:15,628
But to tell the truth,

27
00:03:15,628 --> 00:03:18,791
I've already started to get
bored of vacation trips.

28
00:03:22,034 --> 00:03:27,370
Woman of Gold

29
00:03:59,672 --> 00:04:02,903
It doesn't look like a quick fix
is going to work on this.

30
00:04:04,177 --> 00:04:06,112
You'll have to call a repair service.

31
00:04:06,112 --> 00:04:08,014
But I have to go to Trevi!

32
00:04:08,014 --> 00:04:09,515
Trevi?

33
00:04:09,515 --> 00:04:11,217
The Fontana di Trevi?

34
00:04:11,217 --> 00:04:12,718
Yeah...

35
00:04:12,718 --> 00:04:14,320
I'm sorry,

36
00:04:14,320 --> 00:04:16,789
but if you want to hitchhike there,
ask someone else.

37
00:04:16,789 --> 00:04:18,357
I've already been to Rome.

38
00:04:18,357 --> 00:04:20,059
Isn't there any way I can get you to take me?

39
00:04:20,059 --> 00:04:22,027
I'm being chased!

40
00:04:22,728 --> 00:04:25,822
Being chased? By whom?

41
00:04:29,802 --> 00:04:31,235
Sorry...

42
00:04:36,309 --> 00:04:38,539
That's them!

43
00:04:45,918 --> 00:04:47,146
Get in.

44
00:05:00,499 --> 00:05:02,126
Looks like she wasn't lying.

45
00:05:06,572 --> 00:05:08,301
They're aiming for the tires.

46
00:05:08,774 --> 00:05:11,470
They must be more than some local thugs.

47
00:05:12,345 --> 00:05:14,279
What did you do?

48
00:05:42,208 --> 00:05:43,766
Hold on tight!

49
00:06:04,897 --> 00:06:07,024
Look what you made me do.

50
00:06:07,266 --> 00:06:08,563
Thank you.

51
00:06:09,669 --> 00:06:11,728
I'm sure you have a pretty good reason.

52
00:06:13,639 --> 00:06:15,541
If you don't want to say it, that's fine.

53
00:06:15,541 --> 00:06:17,839
I'm not interested in prying into it either.

54
00:06:19,545 --> 00:06:21,914
So we're traveling toward Rome, huh?

55
00:06:21,914 --> 00:06:24,984
All right, I'll just keep going this direction
and take you to Trevi.

56
00:06:24,984 --> 00:06:26,085
You will?

57
00:06:26,085 --> 00:06:29,021
Turning back the other direction would probably
mean running into trouble again anyway.

58
00:06:29,021 --> 00:06:30,022
And besides...

59
00:06:30,022 --> 00:06:31,319
And besides?

60
00:06:35,861 --> 00:06:38,731
I wanted to say "it would be
a great way to kill my boredom,"

61
00:06:38,731 --> 00:06:40,790
but I kept it in.

62
00:06:54,547 --> 00:06:56,378
He should be coming out any time now.

63
00:06:57,616 --> 00:06:58,810
He's on the move.

64
00:07:02,755 --> 00:07:06,748
No doubt about it, he's going to keep
heading toward Rome, 9-4.

65
00:07:17,002 --> 00:07:18,304
Roger.

66
00:07:18,304 --> 00:07:22,001
Good work, 9-7. I'll take it from here.

67
00:07:32,218 --> 00:07:36,154
Those damn Western Bloc bitches.
They're so irritating.

68
00:07:43,329 --> 00:07:44,397
Say...

69
00:07:44,397 --> 00:07:45,731
What?

70
00:07:45,731 --> 00:07:49,360
In a situation like this,
I wonder if we should talk?

71
00:07:49,535 --> 00:07:51,804
You're trying to be nice now?

72
00:07:51,804 --> 00:07:55,535
You don't really have to.
I don't like chatting either.

73
00:07:55,808 --> 00:07:57,332
Oh...

74
00:07:57,943 --> 00:08:00,513
But you could tell me your name.

75
00:08:00,513 --> 00:08:02,174
I don't know what to call you.

76
00:08:03,115 --> 00:08:04,742
My name?

77
00:08:05,651 --> 00:08:08,142
It's all right, you don't have to say that either.

78
00:08:10,689 --> 00:08:13,959
It doesn't particularly seem like she's hiding it.

79
00:08:13,959 --> 00:08:16,128
Could she be...

80
00:08:16,128 --> 00:08:18,528
air-headed?

81
00:08:23,769 --> 00:08:25,396
I'm going to stop for a minute.

82
00:08:30,810 --> 00:08:34,007
I can at least do this much for you.
To show my thanks.

83
00:08:34,847 --> 00:08:37,873
Really? Then please do.

84
00:08:41,554 --> 00:08:44,921
I'm sorry. It looks like they won't take this coin.

85
00:08:45,024 --> 00:08:46,425
Would you give me change for it?

86
00:08:46,425 --> 00:08:47,653
Sure.

87
00:08:47,860 --> 00:08:49,293
Use this.

88
00:08:49,829 --> 00:08:51,130
Thanks.

89
00:08:51,130 --> 00:08:52,064
Here you go.

90
00:08:52,064 --> 00:08:54,430
Huh? You don't have to...

91
00:09:11,317 --> 00:09:12,750
Are they here?

92
00:09:13,953 --> 00:09:15,352
No.

93
00:09:27,867 --> 00:09:29,391
She's here.

94
00:09:36,542 --> 00:09:38,476
Damn, stubborn bitch.

95
00:09:40,579 --> 00:09:42,314
Why don't you try this?

96
00:09:42,314 --> 00:09:45,545
They say if you toss two coins in,
you'll be united with the one you love.

97
00:09:46,185 --> 00:09:48,210
You might be able to meet the person
you're waiting for.

98
00:09:48,487 --> 00:09:49,681
Like this?

99
00:09:49,788 --> 00:09:52,120
Now that I think about it,
that was my second one,

100
00:09:53,859 --> 00:09:56,487
even though there's no one for me
to be united with.

101
00:09:58,531 --> 00:10:01,557
Is that the best I can do for a partner?

102
00:10:07,907 --> 00:10:10,569
How can I give that woman the slip?

103
00:10:13,879 --> 00:10:17,838
What do you think? I'll give it to you cheap,
as a memento from your trip.

104
00:10:18,651 --> 00:10:20,278
Don't go taking my picture without permission!

105
00:10:22,788 --> 00:10:24,490
Hey, wait a minute!

106
00:10:24,490 --> 00:10:25,582
Huh?

107
00:10:36,969 --> 00:10:40,336
What are you doing in a place like this, 9-4?

108
00:10:43,776 --> 00:10:46,579
Can't you tell? I'm on a mission.

109
00:10:46,579 --> 00:10:49,281
I'm tailing an Eastern Bloc courier,

110
00:10:49,281 --> 00:10:51,340
the open-air café in the back on your right.

111
00:10:54,253 --> 00:10:57,122
Him, huh? Are you sure?

112
00:10:57,122 --> 00:10:58,824
We know his identity.

113
00:10:58,824 --> 00:11:00,626
His name is Borzov.

114
00:11:00,626 --> 00:11:04,363
The goods are probably in that attaché case,

115
00:11:04,363 --> 00:11:06,465
but that's actually the only thing
we haven't been able to confirm.

116
00:11:06,465 --> 00:11:07,399
Want me to help?

117
00:11:07,399 --> 00:11:08,934
Don't be silly.

118
00:11:08,934 --> 00:11:12,338
I'm not going to ask for help from someone
on vacation. I'm not that rude.

119
00:11:12,338 --> 00:11:13,600
And besides...

120
00:11:13,939 --> 00:11:15,708
You have a friend with you, don't you?

121
00:11:15,708 --> 00:11:17,109
Friend?

122
00:11:17,109 --> 00:11:19,912
Oh yeah, I just met her, that's all.

123
00:11:19,912 --> 00:11:24,450
How do I put it...
She's airheaded, or maybe kind of pure.

124
00:11:24,450 --> 00:11:26,918
Pure? What do you mean by that?

125
00:11:29,188 --> 00:11:30,655
He's on the move.

126
00:11:37,529 --> 00:11:38,962
Later.

127
00:11:50,776 --> 00:11:52,444
So are things settled now?

128
00:11:52,444 --> 00:11:54,309
Well, that's what it looks like.

129
00:12:01,587 --> 00:12:06,251
And so, all was right with the world.
It was all kind of anti-climactic.

130
00:12:06,659 --> 00:12:09,856
And I was ready to drive away from Rome
for real for the second time, but...

131
00:12:13,265 --> 00:12:14,857
I'm being followed?

132
00:12:44,997 --> 00:12:46,931
This is a one-way street the whole way.

133
00:12:47,199 --> 00:12:48,860
No chance for me to dodge them.

134
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:10,622
Yeah, we've got her cornered.

135
00:13:10,622 --> 00:13:14,058
It sucks for the Eastern Bloc,
but that woman is Golden Bat's now.

136
00:13:15,894 --> 00:13:19,193
Wh... Who are you?

137
00:13:19,732 --> 00:13:21,934
So you did think I was someone else after all.

138
00:13:21,934 --> 00:13:24,198
Seems like you were after that woman.

139
00:13:24,269 --> 00:13:25,671
Tell me.

140
00:13:25,671 --> 00:13:29,198
Why would Golden Bat go to such overblown
measures against a single woman?

141
00:13:29,641 --> 00:13:31,836
Who is that woman, anyway?

142
00:13:44,456 --> 00:13:46,356
I knew it: A transmitter.

143
00:13:46,492 --> 00:13:48,619
Golden Bat was following this.

144
00:14:04,409 --> 00:14:05,911
How about it?

145
00:14:05,911 --> 00:14:10,280
A Venus standing in front of the Foro Romano
in the evening, with a sad look on her face.

146
00:14:10,349 --> 00:14:12,112
I'll sell it to you for cheap.

147
00:14:13,452 --> 00:14:14,186
It's you...

148
00:14:14,186 --> 00:14:14,553
Huh?
It's you...

149
00:14:14,553 --> 00:14:14,951
Huh?

150
00:14:21,126 --> 00:14:26,325
A man told me to tell you
to go to the Colosseum, that's all.

151
00:14:26,398 --> 00:14:27,533
A man?

152
00:14:27,533 --> 00:14:31,401
A gloomy-looking man sitting
in the corner of the open-air café.

153
00:14:32,437 --> 00:14:33,870
Borzov...

154
00:14:34,439 --> 00:14:36,134
I have to inform 9-4.

155
00:14:55,627 --> 00:14:58,255
The sound of the safety on a laser gun
being released...

156
00:14:59,198 --> 00:15:00,722
Someone's here.

157
00:15:08,440 --> 00:15:09,174
9-4!

158
00:15:09,174 --> 00:15:10,641
9-1!

159
00:15:10,976 --> 00:15:12,277
Are you wounded?

160
00:15:12,277 --> 00:15:14,546
It's something more pathetic than a wound.

161
00:15:14,546 --> 00:15:17,071
I got hit right in the leg shaft.

162
00:15:17,716 --> 00:15:19,081
What about Borzov?

163
00:15:19,451 --> 00:15:24,389
I just couldn't figure out what it is
he's trying to transport out.

164
00:15:24,389 --> 00:15:27,984
I drove him hard into a corner,
which was all well and good, but...

165
00:15:28,493 --> 00:15:31,063
W... Wait! Don't shoot!

166
00:15:31,063 --> 00:15:33,565
Hand over the attaché case.

167
00:15:33,565 --> 00:15:36,568
I don't know what it is you're
trying to transport out,

168
00:15:36,568 --> 00:15:38,832
but I'm not going to stand by and
let you take it out of the Western Bl-

169
00:15:43,442 --> 00:15:45,137
Dammit...

170
00:15:49,681 --> 00:15:52,445
Borzov couldn't have gotten far either.

171
00:15:53,018 --> 00:15:54,686
Who was it who hit you from behind?

172
00:15:54,686 --> 00:15:56,321
I don't know.

173
00:15:56,321 --> 00:15:57,948
I was careless.

174
00:15:58,156 --> 00:15:59,623
That woman...

175
00:16:00,392 --> 00:16:02,794
Give me a laser gun attachment.

176
00:16:02,794 --> 00:16:05,126
The most powerful one you've got.

177
00:16:05,530 --> 00:16:07,498
A powerful one?

178
00:16:09,234 --> 00:16:11,236
I have a small Napalm one, but...

179
00:16:11,236 --> 00:16:12,897
Who exactly are you going after?

180
00:16:15,340 --> 00:16:17,001
Just someone I know.

181
00:16:24,416 --> 00:16:25,883
Come on out!

182
00:16:27,319 --> 00:16:28,752
I know you're there!

183
00:16:33,659 --> 00:16:36,492
This is how you pay me back
for doing you a favor?

184
00:16:36,561 --> 00:16:37,926
How dare you shoot my partner?!

185
00:16:47,272 --> 00:16:50,764
If you had been trying to trick me,
I would've realized it right away.

186
00:16:51,109 --> 00:16:52,576
Trick you?

187
00:16:52,811 --> 00:16:54,513
That's true.

188
00:16:54,513 --> 00:16:57,516
It's not like you were particularly
trying to trick me.

189
00:16:57,516 --> 00:17:01,687
Your mind isn't capable of thinking up
something as senseless as that; it's pure.

190
00:17:01,687 --> 00:17:05,521
You just chose the best action
to achieve your goal.

191
00:17:28,613 --> 00:17:30,012
I didn't notice.

192
00:17:30,682 --> 00:17:33,352
I never would've guessed you're an android

193
00:17:33,352 --> 00:17:35,252
until Golden Bat told me.

194
00:17:58,176 --> 00:17:59,643
Don't move!

195
00:18:05,617 --> 00:18:08,711
Out with it. What are you trying to transport out?

196
00:18:18,263 --> 00:18:19,252
Huh?

197
00:18:19,498 --> 00:18:20,795
What's this?

198
00:18:34,913 --> 00:18:36,114
Gold?

199
00:18:36,114 --> 00:18:37,849
So that's it.

200
00:18:37,849 --> 00:18:40,317
That's what this man was trying to transport out.

201
00:18:43,555 --> 00:18:45,290
She could be snuck out without
anyone suspecting

202
00:18:45,290 --> 00:18:46,848
that she's actually secret funds
raised in the West.

203
00:18:47,459 --> 00:18:50,485
Not only that, she was equipped with
weapons to protect herself.

204
00:18:50,729 --> 00:18:52,196
A woman of gold...

205
00:18:59,805 --> 00:19:01,966
That's it, get rid of her!

206
00:19:23,929 --> 00:19:25,453
She's gone mad.

207
00:19:41,346 --> 00:19:42,506
This is...

208
00:20:10,509 --> 00:20:12,238
Let me give this back to you too!

209
00:20:41,573 --> 00:20:45,304
The purer gold is,
the better it conducts electricity.

210
00:20:46,845 --> 00:20:50,246
Thank goodness you were pure.

211
00:20:55,654 --> 00:20:57,554
Why Trevi again?

212
00:20:57,789 --> 00:21:00,917
To tell you the truth,
this is my first time in Rome.

213
00:21:01,259 --> 00:21:05,030
I have to go back home now, so I want to
make sure I can come back some time.

214
00:21:05,030 --> 00:21:07,362
Of course, next time it will be as a tourist.

215
00:21:08,233 --> 00:21:11,536
But you know, I was completely fooled
by the attaché case.

216
00:21:11,536 --> 00:21:13,595
I can't believe it was a fake.

217
00:21:13,972 --> 00:21:15,941
I don't know if it was exactly fake.

218
00:21:15,941 --> 00:21:17,075
While doing his courier work,

219
00:21:17,075 --> 00:21:19,509
he was probably just transporting things
that fit his own tastes too.

220
00:21:19,844 --> 00:21:22,047
They have tough inspections
over there after all.

221
00:21:22,047 --> 00:21:23,810
What a scumbag.

222
00:21:29,187 --> 00:21:30,622
Aren't you going to do it too?

223
00:21:30,622 --> 00:21:32,385
I already have.

224
00:21:37,195 --> 00:21:42,394
This was something Golden Bat
placed on the woman of gold.

225
00:21:42,667 --> 00:21:46,171
They found out about her existence and
tried to take her for themselves.

226
00:21:46,171 --> 00:21:48,306
And she gave that transmitter to you?

227
00:21:48,306 --> 00:21:52,444
Right, it was a cold, calculated move.

228
00:21:52,444 --> 00:21:56,278
She didn't have any hesitation or anything,
no emotions, so I couldn't see through her.

229
00:21:56,748 --> 00:21:57,582
Oh!

230
00:21:57,582 --> 00:21:58,917
Hmm?

231
00:21:58,917 --> 00:22:02,546
Nothing, I was just thinking that
that was my third one.

232
00:22:03,588 --> 00:22:07,319
They say if you toss three in,
you can dump your partner.

233
00:22:07,792 --> 00:22:11,997
My silly habit of sticking my nose into trouble

234
00:22:11,997 --> 00:22:14,761
is what I wish I could get rid of.

235
00:22:15,267 --> 00:22:18,668
But evidently, that's impossible.

236
00:23:56,201 --> 00:23:58,203
I haven't seen you in a while, Grandfather.

237
00:23:58,203 --> 00:24:01,306
Crying is what babies do. Isn't that right?

238
00:24:01,306 --> 00:24:02,741
It's all right, I can do it.

239
00:24:02,741 --> 00:24:05,577
Missiles are transported from here.

240
00:24:05,577 --> 00:24:08,012
It was my mistake. Please leave me and run.

241
00:24:08,012 --> 00:24:10,105
Next Mission: "Pop"